From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:19:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep clang 22's lock-order checks as warnings

clang 22 enforces ACQUIRED_BEFORE/ACQUIRED_AFTER under -Wthread-safety
(earlier releases left that to -Wthread-safety-beta), and 23.2's ART
runtime fails it, e.g. "mutex 'mutator_lock_' must be acquired before
'monitor_lock_'" in monitor.cc. Report it without failing the build when
the clang is r596125 or newer.

Change-Id: I20de0db9e01fb411bb634a3ca3ac34d6266cb13f
---
 cc/config/global.go | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cc/config/global.go b/cc/config/global.go
index 57096b8..41b05ee 100644
--- a/cc/config/global.go
+++ b/cc/config/global.go
@@ -515,6 +515,9 @@ func init() {
 		if ClangVersionAtLeast(ctx, 596125) {
 			flags = append(flags, "-Wno-incompatible-pointer-types")
 			flags = append(flags, "-Wno-c2y-extensions")
+			// clang 22 checks acquired_before/after ordering under plain
+			// -Wthread-safety; 23.2's ART is not annotated for it.
+			flags = append(flags, "-Wno-error=thread-safety-analysis")
 		}
 		if ctx.Config().IsEnvTrue("LLVM_NEXT") {
 			flags = append(noOverrideGlobalCflags, llvmNextExtraCommonGlobalCflags...)
